WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:11.052
In tutorial 10.2, you'll see what your
credits pay for, and when they expire.

00:00:12.185 --> 00:00:16.946
First, click your credits in the sidebar.
They open Credits, in Company settings.

00:00:18.639 --> 00:00:22.934
At the top is your balance, and about
how long it lasts at the rate you use it.

00:00:25.139 --> 00:00:27.714
Available now is what you can spend.

00:00:27.764 --> 00:00:31.951
Held by running analyses is set
aside until each one finishes.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:37.045
Kept for autopilot is saved for
your websites' automatic work.

00:00:37.095 --> 00:00:39.416
Used this month adds up what's gone.

00:00:40.495 --> 00:00:46.065
Next, This month splits your use in two.
Autopilot is your websites' automatic work,

00:00:46.115 --> 00:00:48.650
and on-demand is the analyses you start.

00:00:49.623 --> 00:00:54.173
Autopilot by website shows what each
website is forecast to use a month,

00:00:54.223 --> 00:00:55.816
and what it's used so far.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:01.833
Below, see your use by feature, and day
by day, so you know where your credits go.

00:01:04.169 --> 00:01:08.879
Then, Your credits lists where each
batch came from, and when it expires.

00:01:08.929 --> 00:01:11.315
The soonest to expire are used first.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:16.880
How credits work sums up the rules.
Every analysis shows its price first,

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.709
and one that fails is free.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:24.480
Finally, Activity lists every
credit added and used, newest first.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.709
Choose On-demand to see only
the analyses you started.

00:01:28.693 --> 00:01:32.241
Click Download CSV to keep
the list in a spreadsheet.

00:01:34.218 --> 00:01:38.420
Now you know what you have, what each
website uses, and when to top up.

00:01:40.718 --> 00:01:45.543
So, read your balance, check this month
and each website, see when credits expire,

00:01:45.593 --> 00:01:47.022
and review the activity.

00:01:47.996 --> 00:01:53.144
You know your credits. Next, buy
credits and set limits in tutorial 10.3.
